<TextPage title="About vectradev" description="vectradev makes free, private image tools that run in your browser, built for the forms people in India fill every day.">
  <p>
    vectradev makes small, fast tools for a common problem: an online form rejects your photo or signature because it is the wrong size. Exam, bank, job and admission portals each have their own rules for pixels, kilobytes and formats, and a photo straight from a phone almost never fits.
  </p>
  <h2>How it works</h2>
  <p>
    Every tool runs inside your web browser. When you choose a photo, it is processed on your own phone or computer and the result is saved straight back to it. Nothing is sent to us, which keeps your documents private and makes the tools work even on a slow connection.
  </p>
  <h2>How we keep exam sizes accurate</h2>
  <p>
    Each exam page shows the date its sizes were last checked and the notification or summary they came from. Exams change their rules from time to time; if you spot a difference, use the <em>Report an outdated size</em> link on that page or write to us, and we will update it.
  </p>
  <h2>Free to use</h2>
  <p>The tools are free. We may show a small number of ads to cover running costs. They are never placed beside upload or download buttons.</p>
</TextPage>
